  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.89",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For $n>39$, is it true that the number of conjugacy classes in the symmetric group $S_n$ of degree $n$ is never a divisor of the order of $S_n$? In other words, is it true that, for $n>39$, the number $p(n)$ of integer partitions of $n$ is never a divisor of $n!$?",
